<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Vienna Award</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1938</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> Award was an arbitration by Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascist-italy">Fascist Italy</a>, announced in Vienna on 2 November 1938, that transferred southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a> and the south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-ruthenia">Carpathian Ruthenia</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. It followed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich-agreement">Munich Agreement</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzhhorod">Uzhhorod</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mukachevo">Mukachevo</a> went to Hungary, forcing the autonomous Carpatho-Ukrainian government to move to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khust">Khust</a>; the award was annulled after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-vienna-award.jpg" alt="First Vienna Award" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jxxy · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Territorial_gains_of_Hungary_1938-41_en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
